<item>
            <title>[LU-20858] lnetctl route show accepts an invalid network name and exits 0</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20858</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Description&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
lnetctl route show does not validate the network name passed to --net. The same argument is rejected by lnetctl net show with a parse error. route show returns success and no output, so a typo in the network name looks like a successful query that found no routes.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Actualresult&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Actual result&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
route show exits 0 with no output on stdout and no output on stderr for an unparseable network name. net show with the same value exits 234 and prints cannot parse net.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;ExpectedResult&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Expected Result&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
lnetctl route show rejects a network name that cannot be parsed, with the same parse error that net show reports, and exits non-zero.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;StepsToReproduce&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Steps To Reproduce&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
1. Ask route show for a network name that cannot be parsed, and check the exit code and the output:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$ lnetctl route show --net nosuchnet
$ echo $?
0
(stdout: 0 bytes, stderr: 0 bytes)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. The same argument passed to net show is rejected:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;{{}}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$ lnetctl net show --net nosuchnet
show:
- &#160; &#160; net:
&#160; &#160; &#160; errno: -2
&#160; &#160; &#160; descr: ! &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;cannot parse net&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
$ echo $?
234&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{{}}&lt;br/&gt;
3. Repeat run of route show with the same unparseable network name:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
$ lnetctl route show --net nosuchnet
$ echo $?
0
(stdout: 0 bytes, stderr: 0 bytes)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
